# The engine set the gate tests against: branch AND commit (re-audit 16.10.2026, AK 5).
#
# Read by .github/scripts/fetch-engine.sh, which every job that installs the engine uses — PHPUnit, Behat, the
# interface and worker end-to-end runs, the acceptance measurements. The branch says which line, the commit which
# state of it; the commit is what makes two runs of the same plugin commit comparable: the engine's branches move
# several times a day (19.11.2026: 07:18 and 23:22; 20.11.2026: 09:37–09:45), and a job that took whatever head it
# found would test another engine than the job before it, with nothing in the plugin changed. Every job writes the
# commits it actually tested into its engine manifest (artifact "engine-manifest-…").
#
# Three sets, three files:
#   engine-pins.env           release   this file: the set a release of CatQuizLab is accepted on;
#   engine-pins-candidate.env candidate the branch heads at the moment of the run, not pinned — the early warning
#                                       that a new engine state breaks the lab, recorded in the manifest;
#   engine-pins-previous.env  previous  the release set before this one — the upgrade test starts there
#                                       (attempts open across the engine upgrade, #136 AK 7) and the cost
#                                       comparison measures against it.
#
# To move the set forward: install the new heads, run catquizlab's PHPUnit suite, the smoke and the engine-session
# test against them, check the engine's CHANGELOG (status codes, stop codes, progress format, validity reasons);
# then copy this file to engine-pins-previous.env and replace the SHAs here, in one commit.
#
# Moved 20.11.2026 (CatQuizLab 0.7.73) to the heads of that morning: local_catquiz 2026111707 / 2026111708 with the
# new stop codes (status 12 "error", 13 "stopscalescomplete"; host codes scalescomplete, noeligiblebeforeminimum),
# the runtime pool with revisions (#146), and the release engine's warm pool no longer blind to deactivated items.

